 "verdict": "NO MOVE \u2014 P(A=4) has the SAME sign as A=2 and A=3 (all negative; A2=-1 A3=-1 A4=-1). The 2nd-order Magnus pairing is sign-STABLE across the deuteron, triton and alpha particle: A=2,3,4 all negative. This strengthens the A=3 finding \u2014 the 'flips positive at A\u22653' reading fails not just at the triton but at \u2074He too \u2014 and makes a constant-sign Magnus carrier the working hypothesis through the light nuclei. Control tr_M(\u03a9\u2082)=0 holds; per-partition sign-indefinite (26+/49-). scope-(a): dimensionless SIGN datum; NOT a MeV (open \u0394_\u03bb gate), NOT a physical binding-sign convention (qou-v7ro/#6077, cited not re-derived).",
 "scope": "scope-(a): decides the A=4 SIGN of tr_M(\u03c1\u00b7\u03a9\u2082) and its place in the sign-vs-A map (A=2,3,4). Dimensionless structural datum. Does NOT reproduce any MeV (open \u0394_\u03bb gate \u2014 a number would be a fit). Does NOT assert a physical binding-sign convention (qou-v7ro / PR #6077, cited not re-derived). No fit; nothing inverted; nothing wired.",
 "wired": false,
 "notes": "Sparse/matrix-free route (owner directive 2026-08-30) extending the A=2 deuteron (qou-dp32) and A=3 triton (PR #6107) Magnus-sign probes to the alpha particle (H\u2081\u2082). Same construction; feasible only because block-diagonal generators + far-commutativity + matrix-free trace avoid the dense 7700\u00b2 OOM. \u2074He word atom_braid_word_3A(2,2) (qou-oppb). Cites qou-v7ro/#6077 for the sign convention.",
